                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "**Title: A New Beginning? More Like the Same Old Garbage.**\n\n**Rating: 1/10 — Not Recommended 👎**\n\nIt's honestly impressive how a game can survive this long and still feel like an unfinished disaster.\n\n**Infestation: The New Beginning** is a perfect example of wasted potential, questionable decisions, and developers who seem completely disconnected from what makes a survival game enjoyable.\n\nThe gameplay feels outdated, the gunplay is clunky, the PvP is frustrating, and the entire experience feels like something that should have been left behind a decade ago.\n\nThe biggest problems?\n\n- **Cheaters and questionable PvP:** Nothing kills a survival game faster than feeling like you're fighting the game itself instead of other players.\n- **Outdated mechanics:** Movement, shooting, animations, and overall gameplay feel painfully behind modern standards.\n- **Repetitive gameplay:** Loot, die, repeat. Very little depth or meaningful progression to keep things interesting.\n- **Lack of polish:** The game feels like a recycled product rather than something that has genuinely evolved.\n- **Wasted potential:** The concept could have been great, but the execution is consistently disappointing.\n\nAnd the funniest part? They actually called it *The New Beginning.*\n\n**A new beginning would suggest improvement. This feels like the same old problems wearing a different name.**\n\nThere are far better survival games out there, made by developers who actually understand what players expect from the genre.\n\n**Final verdict:** Don't waste your time. Being free-to-play doesn't make a game worth playing. Your time is worth more than this.\n\n**The scariest thing in this zombie survival game isn't the zombies. It's the fact that this mess is still around.**",
